<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Last Supper</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mystical Supper</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Last Supper is the final meal that, in the gospel accounts, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a> shared with his apostles in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> before his crucifixion. The earliest mention is in Paul's first letter to the Corinthians, and the gospels place it in the week of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/passover">Passover</a>. During it Jesus predicts his betrayal and Peter's denial. Paul and the Synoptic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gospels">Gospels</a> relate that Jesus took bread and gave it to those present, which is the scriptural basis of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eucharist">Eucharist</a>, while John tells instead of the washing of the apostles' feet. The three Synoptic Gospels describe a Passover meal, which John seems to disagree with, and scholars propose various ways to reconcile them.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/last-supper.jpg" alt="Last Supper" width="330" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leonardo da Vinci · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Last_Supper_-_Leonardo_Da_Vinci_-_High_Resolution_32x16.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>When the Holy Office objected to the “buffoons, drunken Germans, dwarfs” in Paolo Veronese’s huge <b>Last Supper</b>, he was told to change the painting within three months; he changed only its title, to The Feast in the House of Levi, and no more was said.</blockquote><a href="/movement/counter-reformation">Counter-Reformation · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>The New Testament says that after the <b>Last Supper</b> Jesus and his disciples sang a psalm or hymn before going out to the Mount of Olives, and this may have been the Hallel; Jesus, like any literate Jew of the 1st century, may well have known how to…</blockquote><a href="/songs/hallel">Hallel</a></li><li><blockquote>Leonardo died at Clos Lucé, the manor near Amboise given to him by Francis I. Painter of the Mona Lisa and The <b>Last Supper</b>, he also left thousands of pages of notes on anatomy, engineering and nature.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/may-2">2 May in history</a></li></ul></section>
